 "about": "The fields each OPEN100 sheet's equipment schedule (the strip along the bottom of the drawing) prints for each entry, and what is written in them. null = the field label is printed and the value is left blank; a string = what is printed (XXX is a placeholder). Rotating-style entries print CAPACITY, DISCHARGE, RPM, HP; vessel-style entries print OD, LENGTH, MATERIAL; the deaerator entries print design data with XXX placeholders. The OPEN100 drawings are template drawings, so every value field is blank or a placeholder. Use alongside data/open100_equipment_schedule.json (tags and services); the question engine merges the two.",
 "method": "Read by eye from data/drawings/open100_<sheet>.jpg (bottom schedule strip, enlarged), 2026-10-29, for scripts/question_engine.py. One reader, unverified by a second person. Services are as printed (sheet 2 prints DEAREATOR; spelled DEAERATOR here only for the two deaerator heater entries, whose service line reads DEAERATOR). Sheet 3 also lists CND-HTR-160, which data/open100_equipment_schedule.json omits. Sheet 7 lists FWS-PU-170A/B with service LUBE OIL COOLER: printed that way on the drawing.",
